test_explain_hooks
==================

An extension of EXPLAIN for tests. It registers the option TEST_HOOKS,
which needs ANALYZE, and uses each hook an extension of EXPLAIN has: the
validation of the options, a line on each plan node, a line after the
plan, and the data that each qExec sends to the qDisp with the
statistics of its slice. With TEST_HOOKS each plan node shows "Hooked:
true", and after the plan "QE Reports" lists the segments whose qExecs
reported for each slice, "QE Messages" counts the messages of the
qExecs, each of which the qDisp passes on before its pieces, "Other
Pieces" counts the pieces of data of another name, which each qExec
sends empty, and "Reports of Other Statements" counts the reports that
came with another statement's showstatctx than the explained one.

Each qExec sends its slice, its segment and its qe_identifier, and the
qDisp checks them against those of the message, and that the message
came before its pieces, so a report that reaches the wrong slice fails
the statement. The setting test_explain_hooks.send off makes each qExec
send no piece. The setting test_explain_hooks.bad_piece ("short",
"empty_name", "long_name", "unterminated", "no_length", "negative" or
"truncated") makes each qExec send a malformed piece besides, which the
qDisp must refuse. The counts are kept for one plan at a time, and each
plan of an EXPLAIN, such as one that a rule adds, starts with none; an
EXPLAIN with TEST_HOOKS inside another is not supported.

The qExecs send their data on every EXPLAIN ANALYZE, so the library
must be loaded in every backend that runs the tests, the qExecs' too,
and installed on every host. The setup test sets
session_preload_libraries for the test database, a setting that reaches
every instance, and each test runs in a new session; the teardown test
resets it. The expected output is that of a cluster of three primary
segments, such as the demo cluster. installcheck-world installs the
module and runs its tests; to run them alone against a running cluster:

    make install
    make installcheck
